% load this package instead of stex to build stex files without actually using stex

% This only works if you manually add macro definitions for all stex-generated macros that your document does in fact use.
% That does not scale in general, but it is a good trade-off if your document
% - uses only few stex-generated macros (so that there is little manual work)
% - has a large dependency cone (so that real stex is slow)
% - is compiled a lot

% You can use \newapplied etc. to make defining new macros easier.

